 **R0047 (c0127, prepared after this raft) also changes the run's lock**: every process that records its pid in the lock records its kernel start id with it; a worker's id is the content of its own `pid-<n>` record (c0127 Design, Writers). This raft's launcher record (`REAPER` creating `<lock>/pid-<launcher pid>`) needs the same: if R0047 has landed, the launcher runs `fence.STARTED` for its own pid and writes the id into the file it creates, before closing it. No other file appears in the lock, so this raft's `launcher-lock.spec` (the lock lists exactly `pid-<launcher>`) is unaffected; without the id, R0047's promoted `tests/acceptance/c0127/reuse.spec.luau` recording case fails on this branch (the launcher shows as a worker without an id). If this raft lands first, R0047 adds it. Under bwrap the id lives in the record, so `fence.recordsPid` gates it too. (Note added by R0047's prep, design reviews 004 F1 and 005 F1.)
 
